   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "SAME CHARACTER, SAME POSE, TWO STYLES: BlazBlue vs Dengeki Bunko, same seed.\n\nThis REDRAWS the reference picture in each style: the colours come from her real pixels, the style LoRA\nredraws the lines and shading. 'Character reference' = Cecilia_NetsuII_Reference.png (flat grey background).\n\nTHE MAIN KNOB = denoise in both samplers (same value in both):\n  0.5 = very close to the reference, little style    0.6 = default    0.7-0.75 = strong style, looser details\nLine-art guide (0.35) keeps details in place at high denoise; Pose guide (0.5) keeps the stance.\nIP-Adapter (0.3) only helps the face and colours; above 0.5 it causes glow and colour casts.\n'Pose (write this)' matters little here (the pose comes from the picture); it is for later poses.\nChange BOTH sampler seeds to the same number for other pictures."
   ],
   "title": "READ ME: Netsu VS style test",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
